It drives the Divoom Pixoo 64 displays of the local network through their
official local HTTP API (http://doc.divoom-gz.com/web/#/12). To find them, it
can ask the official Divoom "Find device" service
(https://app.divoom-gz.com/Device/ReturnSameLANDevice), as the Divoom app
does; this can be turned off in the configuration.

The message rendering order (a frame, then text) and the alternative
:9000/divoom_api endpoint of recent firmware follow the observations of the
Home Assistant integration pixoo-homeassistant (MIT,
https://github.com/gickowtf/pixoo-homeassistant); no code was copied.

